# Normalise line endings in the repository; check out native endings.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` lets git detect text and check out LF everywhere except the
# entries below, so a Windows clone does not produce a diff on every line of every file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The files that must keep CRLF to be executed at all on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Generated by `pixi publish` and by rattler-build, and never edited by hand.
*.conda binary
*.tar.bz2 binary

# Lockfiles are generated but must never be merged around: a two-way merge of a lock
# file produces two valid-looking halves and a `bun install` that silently resolves
# something neither side asked for. Same for pixi.lock.
bun.lock -merge
pixi.lock -merge
Cargo.lock -merge

# Anything under these trees is not source, so diffs of it are noise for a reviewer.
# `linguist-generated` is what makes a generated section collapse in a PR diff.
*.svg linguist-generated
CHANGELOG.md linguist-generated
